PATCH 588: the driver-method sites the AZER1 self-play executes carry their register arguments --
aa4e's XOR highlight (and MGA 1290/1335/1350, the XOR outline it dispatches to), 286e's viewport
bind, a547's PL: plate.

board:0014.  Measured with gdb breakpoints on all 66 functions that still dispatch a driver method
arg-less (109 sites, `fist_icall_far((uint32_t)(DAT_1000_c6xx)))()`) and on the 11 short-list sites
the arity audit lists, over one AZER1 self-play run to tick 2100: three of them execute --

  286e  895 x   the display-list object-render pass; its head `di=word[0x156a] ; ax=word[di] ;
                si=di+6 ; di=word[0x794] ; lcall [0x664]` binds the viewport (MGA 3fca: ax = the draw
                segment, si = the surface's clip rect, di = the row-offset table).  Patch 464 wrote
                the head into its comment and dispatched it arg-less: 3fca bound word[0x578..0x588]
                from stack residue on native and from zeros on wasm (EMULATE_FUNCTION_POINTER_CASTS).
  a547  895 x   the PL: plate drawn every frame while word[0x569c] != 0: `mov ax,0 ; call 524e ;
                push ax` saves the font, `call 5313` fetches the colour word whose low byte is the
                outline's AL (`mov bx,0x967c ; lcall [0x61a]`), `pop ax ; call 524e` restores the
                font.  Patch 310 called the outline without AL and restored the font from unaff_CS.
  aa4e    4 x   the element highlight toggle: every register saved, then `lea bx,[bx+4] ; mov al,dl ;
                lcall [0x626]` -- MGA 1290, the XOR rect outline, over the element's rect in colour
                DL.  Ghidra kept only 1290's 2d6d prologue ("does not return"), so the port never
                drew a single XOR frame; 1335/1350 (the [0x62a]/[0x62e] insets by 1 and 2) host-
                deref'd the rect.  The 22 callers each set DL by an immediate (`mov dl,IMM ; call
                aa4e`) and leave BX = the node the dispatching walk published at DGROUP:0x3e08;
                the immediate is now the second argument at every site.

  MGA 1290 is transcribed instruction-for-instruction (0x1290-0x12de + the run primitives 0x12df
  horizontal / 0x130e vertical: top row, left column, bottom row, right column, the rect words
  swapped in place and restored exactly as the asm does; rowtab = word[0x794], fb descriptor =
  DGROUP:word[0x724], the bases 11db/patch 138 uses).

  The AZER1 self-play still resolves DEFEAT at tick 5357 (5358 before); the heading at tick 2100 now
  differs (002 vs 089) because the object-render pass sees a bound viewport -- the oracle comparison
  of board:0017 is the judge of which is the original's.

